Z||000006||TOM||07-05-2000||11:12 AM||||Its not my ad. I found it for you guys. Yes that thing in the opening is a plastic removable thing. But it sits against a part that is removed. There is a wall covering the opening to hold that thing up.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Lou Christopher||07-05-2000||11:44 AM||||I really need to improve the cooling on my 350 Fiero.  Would this scoop mounted with the opening toward the windsheild help.  I am a little confused by the last note on this that said the part in the opening was removable but there was something behind it.  Can you open this scoop to let air out.  Any help would be appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||DXR_DAD||07-05-2000||09:25 PM||||Lou, Tom's scoop is mounted on the rear deck lid (opening to back of the car) this is just like the rear vents. These are to let hot air escape the engine compartment  (the scoop)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>The air moving over the top of the car creates a vacuum that pulls the hot air out through the vents also cold air under the car is sucked up through the engine compartment and exits the scoop & vents.<P>I hope this helps.<BR>This is Tom's scoop:<P>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=99075&a=723601&p=18231066&Sequence=1">  <P>The opening is not blocked off and there is a hole in the deck lid under that scoop.<P><BR>DXR_DAD<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com/dxr" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroproject.com/dxr</A> <p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 07-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haze_Performance||07-05-2000||10:33 PM||||Its about time for me to say something. Being the "Mr.Mustang" guy I am, The week before I bought my Fiero I sold 4 New Mustang hood scoops  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> .. I never knew that they would come in use for a Fiero.Right now Im tring to work out a deal with a guy at Ford to get me a few more.<P>P.S. Ford still has some in a storage warehouse. My buddy just picked up 8 orignal 1970 Mach 1 hoods (Brand New) for $300.00 total. He just sold ONE to a guy for $825.00<P>------------------<BR>Carl (85 Fiero) My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>Haze Mustang Performance</A>   &  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A>||||reg||2
